  "question": "Task Scheduling System or Batch Processing System Requirements Description:\nThe Task Scheduling or Batch Processing system is used to manage and record the execution status, parameters, and batch information of tasks. Its main features include:\n1.Task Execution Record: Records the execution ID, start time, end time, task name, exit code, exit message, error message, and last update time for each task. Supports recording the external execution ID and parent task execution ID to facilitate hierarchical task management and tracking.\n2.Task Parameter Management: Records the parameters for each task execution, including parameter name and parameter value, and associates them with the task execution record. This helps in configuring task parameters and querying historical parameters.\n3.Task Batch Management: Records the relationship between task execution and batch execution, including batch ID, batch name, start time, and end time. This helps in managing and querying the execution status of tasks across different batches.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0128\n\nCREATE TABLE `batch_job_execution` (\n  `job_execution_id` bigint(20) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `job_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `exit_code` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `exit_message` varchar(2500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `error_message` varchar(2500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_updated` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `external_execution_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `parent_execution_id` bigint(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`job_execution_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `batch_job_execution_params` (\n  `job_execution_id` bigint(20) NOT NULL,\n  `parameter_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `parameter_value` varchar(2500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`job_execution_id`, `parameter_name`),\n  CONSTRAINT `batch_job_execution_params_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`job_execution_id`) REFERENCES `batch_job_execution` (`job_execution_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `batch_job_instance` (\n  `job_instance_id` bigint(20) NOT NULL,\n  `job_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`job_instance_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `batch_job_execution_instance` (\n  `job_execution_id` bigint(20) NOT NULL,\n  `job_instance_id` bigint(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`job_execution_id`, `job_instance_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `batch_job_execution_instance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`job_execution_id`) REFERENCES `batch_job_execution` (`job_execution_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `batch_job_execution_instance_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`job_instance_id`) REFERENCES `batch_job_instance` (`job_instance_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
